WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:02.002
Nikhil: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:03.570
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.972
between Starbucks in India and the US.

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:07.707
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.278
At a Starbucks in India,

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:15.915
we get our hot coffees in four sizes.

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:17.017
No. 1,

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.486
Nikhil: a short,
Joe: Short,

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.722
Nikhil: a tall,
Joe: tall,

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.557
Nikhil: a grande,
Joe: grande,

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:26.359
and the big boy,

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:28.128
Nihil: a venti.
Joe: venti.

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:29.896
I can't think of a single reason

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.998
you would order a coffee of this size.

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:35.101
Who is putting this much
caffeine in their body?

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.270
Me, Nikhil. Me.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:41.174
Let's measure this to see if
it has as much as it should.

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:42.509
Joe: Whoa, wait a second.

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:45.445
Starbucks, I'm disappointed.

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:48.415
It's close. It's 18 ounces, ish.

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:49.949
All right, if I'm paying
this kind of money,

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:53.219
I want a bang for my
buck. 20 ounces to the T.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.254
I think that's 20.

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:55.822
I was about to dunk on Starbucks,

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:57.991
but they actually gave
us the 20 they promised.

00:00:57.991 --> 00:00:59.092
Cheers.

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:05.899
Ah.

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:08.668
Look into the eyes

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:11.438
of an insane caffeine addict.

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:15.208
My vision has just gone blurry.

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:17.777
India's iced coffee comes in three sizes.

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:20.246
Both: Tall.

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:23.383
Grande.

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:26.252
Venti.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:29.923
And an even bigger one, we got the trenta.

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:35.862
I want to mention now
that our venti iced size

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:38.498
is bigger than our venti hot size.

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:40.333
The venti hot was 20 ounces.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.836
This is 24 ounces.

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:44.871
And, of course, let's measure it.

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:47.073
Nikhil: Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:48.808
Can't believe we have done this.

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:51.211
It's not even 16 ounces, Starbucks.

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:52.912
And this has ice in it,

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.647
which should melt and
give you more liquid.

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:57.083
Is that how fluid dynamics works?

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.351
Maybe not.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:01.254
But my disappointment is palpable.

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:03.556
Yeah, I'm gonna go 22 ounces.

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.258
I don't know. It's 2 ounces. That's fine.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:06.493
[laughing]

00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:07.861
It's totally not a big deal.

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:09.329
That's, like, two sips.

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:10.430
I can't speak for anyone else,

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:12.732
but already my bladder is about to burst.

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:15.902
So maybe I don't need 24 more
ounces in my bloodstream.

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:18.071
If that wasn't exciting enough,

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:20.273
we of course have our biggest iced size,

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:23.610
which is the trenta. 30 fluid ounces.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.979
The bladder buster.

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:28.515
This is for anyone who wants to spend

00:02:28.515 --> 00:02:30.517
most of their day in the bathroom.

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:33.219
So you think, what, 28?

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:34.554
Again, 2 ounces off.

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:37.357
You know, Starbucks, 4
ounces more won't kill you.

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:41.227
Ah, this is actually pretty good.

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:43.396
Starbucks actually good? What the hell?

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:44.564
Anyone who watches "Food Wars" knows

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:46.266
we use this measuring cup for everything.

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:48.668
And I know I don't clean it,

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:50.270
and I don't think Joe's cleaning it,

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:52.005
and I don't think Yuelei's cleaning it.

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:54.807
So this thing, never
been cleaned -- yeah, mm.

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:56.709
And of course, if you're in the mood

00:02:56.709 --> 00:03:01.014
for 96 fluid ounces of Starbucks coffee,

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:03.583
ba-bam!

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:06.419
Get yourself the coffee traveler,

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:09.489
aka what Joe drinks in an afternoon.

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:11.457
Here in India, we don't
have a huge coffee traveler.

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:13.626
We just have this little guy.

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:16.996
It's an India-edition
tiny pet coffee traveler.

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:20.033
It's got a lot of cool
India iconography on it.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:23.670
There's a batsman, there is an elephant,

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:25.638
all sorts of cool Indian stuff.

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:29.275
And you can put in 355
ml of coffee in here,

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:32.845
which is around 11.83 ounces of coffee,

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:34.447
roughly a tall.

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:37.016
So, the perfect size.

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:40.853
We also have 1-liter bottles
for iced latte and cold brew.

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:43.022
Word on the street is
they contain 1 liter each,

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:45.358
or 33.8 fluid ounces.

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:48.027
It is so weird using the
US system of measurement.

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:52.198
I'm so used to our normal,
correct metric system.

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:55.635
But let's not start an actual
war over here. Sorry, Joe.

00:03:55.635 --> 00:03:57.670
Yeah, um, I don't care.

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:00.974
Let's take a look at calories.

00:04:00.974 --> 00:04:05.044
A hot venti latte in
India is 289 calories.

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:07.146
For comparison, a normal serving

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:09.649
of dal chawal is 200 calories.

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:12.819
[sighs]

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:15.388
In the US, the same venti café latte

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:17.056
is 250 calories.

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:22.061
So it looks like the US
has 13.5% less calories.

00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:26.366
It's at that temperature where
it's, like, room temperature.

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:27.367
[Windows shutdown music]

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:29.102
My brain is Swiss cheese.

00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:31.170
Everything I say is idiotic.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.939
A hot venti mocha,

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:34.574
which is also what my friends call me,

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:36.943
is 473 calories.

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:40.346
And in the US, our venti
mocha is 450 calories.

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:42.749
So, according to my math, once again,

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:45.885
that's a calorie decrease of 4.9%.

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:48.054
What do you think of that, hot venti boy?

00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:50.690
OK, Joe, it's not a competition.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.325
Let's just try something a little sweeter,

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:55.428
like this venti caramel Frappuccino,

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:58.431
which looks, uh, decadent,
to say the least.

00:04:59.866 --> 00:05:04.103
Oh, my God, that is so sweet.

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:06.239
602 calories.

00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:08.975
And I can feel every single
one of them in each sip.

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:12.045
OK, genuinely, I have
had spoonfuls of sugar

00:05:12.045 --> 00:05:14.314
that are more savory than this drink.

00:05:14.314 --> 00:05:17.250
How can you make something
sweeter than sugar?

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.384
How?

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:23.122
That's a lot of calories, my man.

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:27.060
Ours is 470 calories,
which is also 24 ounces.

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.594
Now, I should note, in the US,

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:31.197
the calories listed on
Starbucks.com are, quote,

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:32.732
"based on standard recipes

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:34.834
and do not reflect customizations."

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:38.771
Get this out of my face. I hate this.

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:40.440
Why is this so -- and they put, like,

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:41.541
they load the syrup in here.

00:05:41.541 --> 00:05:43.209
How can a human being drink one of these?

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:44.410
I don't understand.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:48.348
And now, our most calorific overall drink

00:05:48.348 --> 00:05:49.549
that we have here in India,

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:52.618
a venti strawberry and crème Frappuccino,

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:54.921
963 calories.

00:05:56.489 --> 00:05:57.523
Oh, my God.

00:05:57.523 --> 00:05:58.958
I didn't even think it was possible

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:01.027
to experience a sugar rush

00:06:01.027 --> 00:06:03.930
and a coffee caffeine
high at the same time.

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:07.400
At 963 calories, this is nearly 50%

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:09.702
of your daily caloric intake.

00:06:09.702 --> 00:06:11.871
So please drink this at your own risk.

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:13.840
And I am a risk-taker.

00:06:14.774 --> 00:06:15.808
Whew.

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:18.945
I feel transported to another dimension

00:06:18.945 --> 00:06:21.280
where everything is more colorful

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:23.816
and I can taste sound.

00:06:23.816 --> 00:06:24.884
I don't know. I feel like

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:26.152
we should have an ambulance ready

00:06:26.152 --> 00:06:28.354
if I'm going to finish this drink.

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:30.089
That's a lot of calories, I have to say.

00:06:30.089 --> 00:06:31.557
I'm very impressed.

00:06:31.557 --> 00:06:34.460
Our most highest calorific drink

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:39.065
is the mocha cookie crumble
Frappuccino at the venti size,

00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:42.568
and it's only 590 calories.

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:44.437
Oh, God.

00:06:44.437 --> 00:06:45.638
This looks so bad.

00:06:47.707 --> 00:06:50.410
Oh, man. It's so powerful.

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:51.978
Like, it's so sweet

00:06:51.978 --> 00:06:53.846
that everything from here
on for the rest of my life

00:06:53.846 --> 00:06:55.181
is just going to taste like paper.

00:06:56.916 --> 00:06:58.184
So, what about the cost?

00:06:58.184 --> 00:07:01.587
This venti Frappuccino
will cost you 390 rupees,

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:05.825
which at the time of
filming this video is $5.14.

00:07:05.825 --> 00:07:08.761
In the US, a venti caramel Frappuccino

00:07:08.761 --> 00:07:10.763
is $5.45,

00:07:10.763 --> 00:07:13.900
or about 413 Indian rupees.

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:17.103
Now, I want to point out
that this is 24 ounces

00:07:17.103 --> 00:07:19.739
and not the India 20-ounce venti.

00:07:19.739 --> 00:07:21.908
So if we break it down per fluid ounce,

00:07:21.908 --> 00:07:26.646
it's about 11.5% cost per
fluid ounce decrease in the US.

00:07:26.646 --> 00:07:29.248
Let me give you some context
about Starbucks in India.

00:07:29.248 --> 00:07:32.618
They are catering to
the rich and the elite,

00:07:32.618 --> 00:07:35.321
because it is very expensive over here.

00:07:35.321 --> 00:07:36.422
In South India, where I'm from,

00:07:36.422 --> 00:07:38.691
you can get a filter coffee
for less than 40 rupees,

00:07:38.691 --> 00:07:42.495
which is a fraction of a
dollar, and it's delicious.

00:07:42.495 --> 00:07:45.598
Starbucks would cost you upwards of $5,

00:07:45.598 --> 00:07:48.301
and that's unaffordable for most of India.

00:07:50.036 --> 00:07:52.405
Here is everything that
you can find in a menu

00:07:52.405 --> 00:07:55.374
at an Indian Starbucks that
you won't get in the US.

00:07:55.374 --> 00:07:56.375
Quick clarification.

00:07:56.375 --> 00:07:59.645
Some of the items we have
here are location-specific

00:07:59.645 --> 00:08:02.448
and specific to the season
that we're ordering them.

00:08:02.448 --> 00:08:04.717
It's currently summer here in Mumbai,

00:08:04.717 --> 00:08:07.286
and some of these items
are store-specific.

00:08:07.286 --> 00:08:09.489
So maybe you won't get
them when you go order,

00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:10.556
but let me know.

00:08:10.556 --> 00:08:12.892
And here's everything you
can only find on the menu

00:08:12.892 --> 00:08:15.695
at a US Starbucks you can't get in India.

00:08:15.695 --> 00:08:17.330
Now, a bit of clarification.

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:19.565
We know Starbucks will
customize drink orders

00:08:19.565 --> 00:08:21.534
and there are thousands of variations

00:08:21.534 --> 00:08:23.135
and special secret menu items.

00:08:23.135 --> 00:08:24.136
Thank you, Starbucks.

00:08:24.136 --> 00:08:27.406
So just to make things
not completely insane,

00:08:27.406 --> 00:08:30.076
these are the official
things on the Starbucks menu

00:08:30.076 --> 00:08:31.911
at both India and the US.

00:08:31.911 --> 00:08:33.646
Cool, and let's go.

00:08:33.646 --> 00:08:36.582
All right, let's begin with
all the hot exclusive drinks,

00:08:36.582 --> 00:08:39.919
starting with salted caramel latte.

00:08:39.919 --> 00:08:41.153
Not bad.

00:08:41.153 --> 00:08:43.689
Stardust mocha.

00:08:43.689 --> 00:08:46.092
Boom, we have clarified, no sparkles.

00:08:46.092 --> 00:08:48.227
Nothing about this screams stardust.

00:08:48.227 --> 00:08:50.429
I don't know what you're
talking about, Starbucks,

00:08:50.429 --> 00:08:52.965
but it tastes good.

00:08:52.965 --> 00:08:56.602
Chai tea, or as we call
it here in India, chai.

00:08:56.602 --> 00:08:58.437
Can I just say, it's a bit of a pet peeve

00:08:58.437 --> 00:09:00.840
when you guys call chai "chai tea."

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:03.409
It's like calling tea "tea tea."

00:09:03.409 --> 00:09:05.211
Let me describe a good chai to you.

00:09:05.211 --> 00:09:07.847
All right, it should be
warm. It should be gingery.

00:09:07.847 --> 00:09:11.217
It should feel like a hug from
your mum in your childhood,

00:09:11.217 --> 00:09:12.685
and it should perk your morning up.

00:09:12.685 --> 00:09:15.054
And it should be under 10
rupees, but this is expensive.

00:09:22.428 --> 00:09:25.197
Hello! It's Crystelle, and
I'm here to talk about chai,

00:09:25.197 --> 00:09:26.999
which is actually my favorite drink.

00:09:26.999 --> 00:09:29.368
Every person has their
own recipe for chai,

00:09:29.368 --> 00:09:31.203
but it's a combination
of spices and black tea

00:09:31.203 --> 00:09:33.372
and some milk, and usually
sweetened with a bit of sugar.

00:09:33.372 --> 00:09:35.274
But for me at home, in my recipe,

00:09:35.274 --> 00:09:37.810
cardamom is the most important spice,

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:40.646
cinnamon, ginger, a pinch of cloves,

00:09:40.646 --> 00:09:43.182
and my secret spice is
a bit of black pepper,

00:09:43.182 --> 00:09:45.651
just to give that lovely,
warming, spicy feeling,

00:09:45.651 --> 00:09:46.686
but it's not savory.

00:09:46.686 --> 00:09:48.821
It's just a lovely blend of spices.

00:09:51.657 --> 00:09:55.127
The flavor is not bad,
but I wouldn't call this,

00:09:55.127 --> 00:09:56.162
I wouldn't call this a chai.

00:09:56.162 --> 00:09:58.197
You know what? This is a chai tea!

00:09:58.197 --> 00:09:59.665
Because it's not quite a chai,

00:09:59.665 --> 00:10:01.300
it's not quite a tea.

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:03.736
Fair enough, Starbucks. It's a chai tea.

00:10:03.736 --> 00:10:05.738
Next up, and the drink
I'm most excited to have,

00:10:05.738 --> 00:10:06.939
thandai spice.

00:10:06.939 --> 00:10:09.408
Now, thandai is consumed
primarily in North India

00:10:09.408 --> 00:10:11.077
in the state of Uttar Pradesh,

00:10:11.077 --> 00:10:12.979
where it's this drink that's sweet.

00:10:12.979 --> 00:10:16.048
It contains spices, it
contains rose petals, saffron,

00:10:16.048 --> 00:10:19.018
and sometimes, optionally,
you can add bhang,

00:10:19.018 --> 00:10:21.420
which is marijuana, and
it's completely free,

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:22.822
legal, and optional to add it.

00:10:22.822 --> 00:10:24.323
And people enjoy it during the festivals

00:10:24.323 --> 00:10:26.459
like Holi and Maha Shivratri.

00:10:26.459 --> 00:10:28.561
What, I'm sorry, did he say that

00:10:28.561 --> 00:10:29.962
that drink has marijuana in it?

00:10:29.962 --> 00:10:31.163
Or you can put weed in it?

00:10:31.163 --> 00:10:32.698
I mean, this is California.

00:10:32.698 --> 00:10:34.734
So if there's a drink you can put weed in,

00:10:34.734 --> 00:10:36.302
you'd think that we would have it, right?

00:10:37.536 --> 00:10:38.938
Not bad!

00:10:38.938 --> 00:10:40.306
It's got little pieces

00:10:40.306 --> 00:10:43.843
of pista and badam and other nuts.

00:10:43.843 --> 00:10:45.177
How did you get thandai right

00:10:45.177 --> 00:10:47.346
and mess up something as simple as a chai?

00:10:47.346 --> 00:10:49.949
USA, we got a lot of hot exclusives.

00:10:49.949 --> 00:10:51.717
I'm going to start all the way down here,

00:10:51.717 --> 00:10:54.387
with something called the caffè misto.

00:10:55.421 --> 00:10:56.255
Bland.

00:10:56.255 --> 00:10:57.123
Moving on.

00:10:57.123 --> 00:10:58.724
Almond honey flat white.

00:10:59.625 --> 00:11:01.160
This flat white I like

00:11:01.160 --> 00:11:03.329
because it has a nice honey flavor to it,

00:11:03.329 --> 00:11:05.398
but straight-up flat whites,
I just, I don't get it.

00:11:05.398 --> 00:11:08.200
Cinnamon dolce latte.

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:09.468
I like it. It's not too sweet.

00:11:09.468 --> 00:11:10.703
A white hot chocolate.

00:11:10.703 --> 00:11:12.338
Hot chocolate? Come on.

00:11:13.205 --> 00:11:14.607
This is, like, really good,

00:11:14.607 --> 00:11:16.809
but I don't know if I could
drink a whole one of those.

00:11:16.809 --> 00:11:19.779
This is the caramel apple spice.

00:11:20.646 --> 00:11:21.480
No, thanks.

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:22.715
Steamed apple juice.

00:11:22.715 --> 00:11:25.151
What? Apple juice?

00:11:25.151 --> 00:11:26.585
Hot apple juice. When are you gonna,

00:11:26.585 --> 00:11:28.988
"Ooh, I want some apple
juice right about now"?

00:11:28.988 --> 00:11:30.222
"I haven't seen you in forever!

00:11:30.222 --> 00:11:31.857
Let's meet up for apple juice."

00:11:31.857 --> 00:11:33.859
Cinnamon dolce crème.

00:11:33.859 --> 00:11:34.860
Ugh!

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:36.495
Steamed milk.

00:11:36.495 --> 00:11:37.329
Eh, barf!

00:11:37.329 --> 00:11:38.531
Vanilla crème.

00:11:38.531 --> 00:11:40.733
When you walk past that ice
cream place in the mall,

00:11:40.733 --> 00:11:43.569
it tastes the way it
smells, like strong vanilla.

00:11:43.569 --> 00:11:45.037
I couldn't imagine having
more than two sips of that.

00:11:45.037 --> 00:11:46.338
Already my stomach's starting to hurt.

00:11:46.338 --> 00:11:47.573
I'm gonna be so sick.

00:11:47.573 --> 00:11:50.042
And now it's time for the cold exclusives.

00:11:50.042 --> 00:11:52.878
I'm not having a caffeine crash at all.

00:11:52.878 --> 00:11:53.846
[error ding]

00:11:53.846 --> 00:11:55.448
The citrus cold brew.

00:11:56.415 --> 00:11:57.416
Citrusy.

00:11:57.416 --> 00:12:01.420
Out of everything, this one has
kind of a nice, mild flavor.

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:03.622
The cocoa chai almond.

00:12:06.392 --> 00:12:08.194
Ooh, I just had such a mild one.

00:12:08.194 --> 00:12:11.931
I took a big sip, and
this one is sweet again.

00:12:11.931 --> 00:12:15.067
Vietnamese caramel cold brew.

00:12:15.067 --> 00:12:16.902
It should typically have condensed milk,

00:12:16.902 --> 00:12:19.472
but this has normal milk,
and it's quite good.

00:12:19.472 --> 00:12:20.906
Nitro cold brew.

00:12:20.906 --> 00:12:22.108
It's basically cold brew,

00:12:22.108 --> 00:12:24.410
but if you press a button,
you drink it faster.

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:25.377
[ba-dum tish]

00:12:25.377 --> 00:12:26.812
Dumb joke.

00:12:26.812 --> 00:12:28.814
It tastes like any other cold brew.

00:12:28.814 --> 00:12:32.718
I'd be interested to know
what the nitrogen process is.

00:12:32.718 --> 00:12:34.386
What is nitro cold brew?

00:12:34.386 --> 00:12:36.422
Well, they add nitrogen to it.

00:12:36.422 --> 00:12:38.023
And you know what that does?

00:12:38.023 --> 00:12:39.058
I have no idea.

00:12:39.992 --> 00:12:42.561
Next up, chocolate truffle cold brew.

00:12:42.561 --> 00:12:45.631
You know, that sounds like
something your child self

00:12:45.631 --> 00:12:47.666
and your adult self would want to combine

00:12:47.666 --> 00:12:49.335
if they had to collaborate on a drink.

00:12:49.335 --> 00:12:50.703
Let's see if it's actually good.

00:12:51.971 --> 00:12:53.906
Absolutely not.

00:12:53.906 --> 00:12:57.777
Oh, my God, stardust mocha again.

00:12:57.777 --> 00:12:58.878
Mm.

00:12:58.878 --> 00:13:01.413
I still don't know what
the hell stardust is.

00:13:01.413 --> 00:13:03.349
There are chunks of something.

00:13:03.349 --> 00:13:05.351
Something otherworldly.

00:13:05.351 --> 00:13:07.787
It's like cookies and cream. It's an Oreo.

00:13:07.787 --> 00:13:09.088
It's an Oreo!

00:13:09.088 --> 00:13:12.758
Thandai spice, same flavor, but now cold.

00:13:12.758 --> 00:13:13.592
Mm,

00:13:13.592 --> 00:13:15.494
hm!

00:13:15.494 --> 00:13:19.131
Too much sugar for one
young man to consume.

00:13:19.131 --> 00:13:20.533
I'm losing it!

00:13:20.533 --> 00:13:22.434
I'm seeing the light.

00:13:22.434 --> 00:13:23.669
Oh, no, I'm literally seeing the light.

00:13:23.669 --> 00:13:24.804
There's a light above me.

00:13:24.804 --> 00:13:25.905
You know, the funny thing is

00:13:25.905 --> 00:13:27.540
thandai is meant to be consumed cold,

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:30.810
so this is the appropriate
temperature and way to drink it.

00:13:30.810 --> 00:13:33.479
But it's layered with
so much whipped cream,

00:13:33.479 --> 00:13:35.381
and it's so sweet.

00:13:35.381 --> 00:13:39.151
Thandai requires a balance
of spices and sweetness,

00:13:39.151 --> 00:13:41.220
and that's what this is lacking.

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:43.289
And the final two drinks
are salted caramel

00:13:43.289 --> 00:13:46.358
and strawberry with cream,
but I already tasted those.

00:13:46.358 --> 00:13:48.894
Maybe it got better with
time, you never know.

00:13:48.894 --> 00:13:50.729
You ought to give everything a chance.

00:13:52.164 --> 00:13:54.300
I'm never giving anything
a chance ever again.

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:56.368
And now for the pre-bottled drinks.

00:13:56.368 --> 00:13:58.437
They've got three of
them in 1-liter bottles.

00:13:58.437 --> 00:14:01.707
This is the iced shaken hibiscus lemonade.

00:14:01.707 --> 00:14:03.409
Looks quite refreshing.

00:14:04.476 --> 00:14:05.477
Mm.

00:14:05.477 --> 00:14:07.379
That is very nice.

00:14:07.379 --> 00:14:09.682
It says it serves four to five cups,

00:14:09.682 --> 00:14:11.483
which, if you're in an Indian family,

00:14:11.483 --> 00:14:13.986
they're going to make this
last for at least 20 people.

00:14:13.986 --> 00:14:15.988
And it's very reminiscent of Rooh Afza,

00:14:15.988 --> 00:14:18.157
which is a rose flavoring
that we add to water,

00:14:18.157 --> 00:14:19.325
and it's super delicious.

00:14:19.325 --> 00:14:21.126
I think this is a good substitute.

00:14:21.126 --> 00:14:23.529
White mocha caramel cold brew.

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:26.065
Oh, my God.

00:14:26.065 --> 00:14:29.235
I've gotten to the stage
where I can smell sugar.

00:14:29.235 --> 00:14:30.669
I can see sugar.

00:14:30.669 --> 00:14:32.171
I can hear sugar.

00:14:32.171 --> 00:14:34.807
I think I am sugar at this point.

00:14:34.807 --> 00:14:36.809
Starbucks signature chocolate.

00:14:36.809 --> 00:14:39.011
Normally I would be
very excited about this,

00:14:39.011 --> 00:14:42.581
but I am so soaked to the
brim with sweet stuff.

00:14:43.582 --> 00:14:44.483
It's actually good.

00:14:44.483 --> 00:14:45.851
It's, like, the amount of chocolate

00:14:45.851 --> 00:14:47.553
you want to put in your cocoa,

00:14:47.553 --> 00:14:50.389
but you know it's
probably not good for you.

00:14:50.389 --> 00:14:53.058
I'm losing my goddamn mind. [laughs]

00:14:53.058 --> 00:14:54.560
All right, starting down here.

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:56.195
Something you can only get in the US

00:14:56.195 --> 00:14:59.665
is the mocha cookie crumble Frappuccino.

00:14:59.665 --> 00:15:02.468
It's looking a little sad.

00:15:02.468 --> 00:15:06.138
So, "Food Wars" tip, bring your own whip.

00:15:07.439 --> 00:15:09.041
That's another one of Joe's tips!

00:15:09.041 --> 00:15:11.710
Mm, I'm not getting the cookie part of it.

00:15:11.710 --> 00:15:13.846
It just tastes like a chocolate milkshake.

00:15:13.846 --> 00:15:15.481
I don't know if that's really
doing much for the flavor.

00:15:15.481 --> 00:15:18.217
The caramel ribbon crunch Frappuccino.

00:15:19.151 --> 00:15:21.020
I don't know how anyone could
drink a whole one of these.

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:22.588
The recommended serving for this, Joe,

00:15:22.588 --> 00:15:24.089
should be, like, two sips.

00:15:24.089 --> 00:15:26.592
It's like, sip No. 2,
and I'm good for a week.

00:15:26.592 --> 00:15:27.426
Ugh.

00:15:27.426 --> 00:15:28.761
The high-fructose corn syrup

00:15:28.761 --> 00:15:30.629
is working overtime in that one.

00:15:30.629 --> 00:15:33.232
The caffè vanilla Frappuccino.

00:15:34.533 --> 00:15:36.302
You know I always keep this thang on me.

00:15:37.169 --> 00:15:39.305
The least objectionable one, I guess.

00:15:39.305 --> 00:15:40.706
Actually a little weak, to be honest.

00:15:40.706 --> 00:15:42.975
Then again, after these two,
maybe it's perfectly fine.

00:15:42.975 --> 00:15:45.311
Nitro, the official cold brew

00:15:45.311 --> 00:15:48.047
of the "Fast and Furious"
franchise, Joseph.

00:15:48.047 --> 00:15:49.949
Just pour this on your
engine, and off you go,

00:15:49.949 --> 00:15:51.617
off you and Vin Diesel go.

00:15:51.617 --> 00:15:53.319
It doesn't require ice.

00:15:53.319 --> 00:15:54.887
Has a smoother flavor, right?

00:15:54.887 --> 00:15:56.355
Now, if you want something
a little bit sweeter

00:15:56.355 --> 00:15:57.323
in your cold brew,

00:15:57.323 --> 00:16:00.559
you can get yourself a vanilla
sweet cream nitro cold brew.

00:16:01.961 --> 00:16:02.928
Joe fucks with it.

00:16:02.928 --> 00:16:04.463
We got a vanilla oat milk,

00:16:04.463 --> 00:16:06.065
we got a brown sugar oat milk,

00:16:06.065 --> 00:16:08.233
and we got a chocolate almond milk.

00:16:08.233 --> 00:16:09.635
Here they are.

00:16:09.635 --> 00:16:11.370
Not as strong of a flavor
as I thought it would be.

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:12.304
Brown sugar.

00:16:13.138 --> 00:16:14.406
I'm definitely tasting it.

00:16:14.406 --> 00:16:15.507
Yeah, not bad.

00:16:15.507 --> 00:16:17.743
I have reason to believe
this was unshooken.

00:16:17.743 --> 00:16:18.744
Think I could shake it without?

00:16:20.646 --> 00:16:23.048
I would recommend this
one out of all three,

00:16:23.048 --> 00:16:25.784
but insist they shake it in front of you.

00:16:25.784 --> 00:16:27.553
You can get yourself an iced flat white

00:16:27.553 --> 00:16:29.421
and an iced honey flat white.

00:16:32.458 --> 00:16:33.292
Skip 'em.

00:16:33.292 --> 00:16:35.160
Iced cinnamon dolce latte

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:38.163
and an iced Starbucks blond latte.

00:16:38.163 --> 00:16:38.998
Not bad.

00:16:40.232 --> 00:16:42.401
Can confirm a sip is good.

00:16:42.401 --> 00:16:43.669
I don't know about a whole one of these.

00:16:43.669 --> 00:16:45.738
Already I'm kind of like, eh.

00:16:45.738 --> 00:16:47.373
Starbuck teas,

00:16:47.373 --> 00:16:49.108
or, as my mum calls them,

00:16:49.108 --> 00:16:50.576
"I can make this at home."

00:16:50.576 --> 00:16:53.612
Starting off with Indian spice majestic.

00:16:53.612 --> 00:16:55.080
Wow, OK.

00:16:55.948 --> 00:16:57.549
Oh! Can I just say,

00:16:57.549 --> 00:16:59.151
drinking this after everything else

00:16:59.151 --> 00:17:01.253
is such a breath of fresh air.

00:17:01.253 --> 00:17:03.088
You know, it's a simple tea,

00:17:03.088 --> 00:17:06.258
but it's very flavorful, very spicy.

00:17:06.258 --> 00:17:07.292
Would recommend.

00:17:07.292 --> 00:17:10.562
Next up, matcha espresso fusion.

00:17:10.562 --> 00:17:13.866
It's part of the trifecta
of three ingredients

00:17:13.866 --> 00:17:15.701
that have become very popular in India.

00:17:15.701 --> 00:17:19.872
Matcha, peri-peri, and red velvet.

00:17:22.374 --> 00:17:26.178
I feel like the espresso counters
the sweetness that it has,

00:17:26.178 --> 00:17:27.579
and the matcha flavor's there.

00:17:27.579 --> 00:17:29.314
Again, just cut down on the sweetness,

00:17:29.314 --> 00:17:31.116
and this would actually be good.

00:17:31.116 --> 00:17:34.853
Now, the exclusive hot teas
you get here in the US.

00:17:34.853 --> 00:17:38.424
The royal English breakfast tea latte,

00:17:38.424 --> 00:17:41.193
London fog tea latte,

00:17:41.193 --> 00:17:43.662
honey citrus mint tea,

00:17:43.662 --> 00:17:46.465
a jade citrus mint brewed tea,

00:17:46.465 --> 00:17:48.901
the mint majesty.

00:17:48.901 --> 00:17:51.303
Mint, matcha, green, all bad.

00:17:51.303 --> 00:17:53.572
The trinity of gross. I don't want it.

00:17:53.572 --> 00:17:55.941
The peach tranquility.

00:17:55.941 --> 00:17:57.376
And they spell it "tranquility,"

00:17:57.376 --> 00:17:59.344
but it should be tranquili-T-E-A.

00:17:59.344 --> 00:18:00.746
I feel like they missed a trick there.

00:18:00.746 --> 00:18:02.414
OK, so those are the two hot teas.

00:18:02.414 --> 00:18:03.949
It's now time for the cold teas,

00:18:03.949 --> 00:18:06.952
starting with an iced green tea.

00:18:06.952 --> 00:18:09.354
I feel like when you
start drinking green tea,

00:18:09.354 --> 00:18:13.192
it's a sign of adulthood,
and there's no going back.

00:18:13.192 --> 00:18:14.293
That's actually pretty good.

00:18:14.293 --> 00:18:15.861
And now I feel old.

00:18:16.862 --> 00:18:19.631
Hibiscus passion lemonade.

00:18:19.631 --> 00:18:21.333
So many ingredients,

00:18:21.333 --> 00:18:23.135
but I know I'm going to taste only sugar.

00:18:23.135 --> 00:18:26.305
Hey, that's pretty good.

00:18:26.305 --> 00:18:28.574
It's kind of flowery, fruity.

00:18:28.574 --> 00:18:29.875
I really like this.

00:18:29.875 --> 00:18:33.145
A maveha espresso fusion.

00:18:33.145 --> 00:18:34.580
Oh, this is an iced matcha?

00:18:34.580 --> 00:18:36.415
Oh, OK, sorry.

00:18:36.415 --> 00:18:37.850
My bad, my bad. It's,

00:18:37.850 --> 00:18:40.085
guys, it's the Starbucks handwriting.

00:18:40.085 --> 00:18:41.620
Honestly, sometimes I think it's just

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:44.389
doctors writing prescriptions
on these coffee mugs.

00:18:44.389 --> 00:18:45.858
By the way, let me know in the comments,

00:18:45.858 --> 00:18:47.926
what's the weirdest way
somebody has spelled your name

00:18:47.926 --> 00:18:49.094
in Starbucks?

00:18:50.062 --> 00:18:53.932
Mm. I prefer this to
the weird hot sweet one.

00:18:53.932 --> 00:18:56.235
Yeah, I like the teas way
more than the coffees.

00:18:56.235 --> 00:18:59.171
So, I don't know what
that says about Starbucks,

00:18:59.171 --> 00:19:01.206
but I'm a fan.

00:19:01.206 --> 00:19:02.608
I feel the exact opposite.

00:19:02.608 --> 00:19:04.009
I do not like tea at all.

00:19:04.009 --> 00:19:06.478
And this is all the
stuff on a Starbucks menu

00:19:06.478 --> 00:19:08.747
I have never gotten and
would like to never get.

00:19:08.747 --> 00:19:10.682
But, gotta do it. It's the job.

00:19:10.682 --> 00:19:12.551
So we will start down here.

00:19:12.551 --> 00:19:15.654
At the Starbucks in the
US, you can get yourself

00:19:15.654 --> 00:19:18.824
iced black tea and an
iced black tea lemonade.

00:19:18.824 --> 00:19:20.159
Moving on, you can get peach teas.

00:19:20.159 --> 00:19:21.493
We got an iced peach green tea

00:19:21.493 --> 00:19:24.196
and an iced peach tea lemonade.

00:19:24.196 --> 00:19:26.632
So, this tastes good because
it's peach and lemonade.

00:19:26.632 --> 00:19:27.599
I don't taste any tea.

00:19:27.599 --> 00:19:31.003
Green iced green tea lemonade.

00:19:31.003 --> 00:19:33.205
Oh, grande, not -- the first GR is grande.

00:19:33.205 --> 00:19:34.840
Grande iced green tea latte.

00:19:34.840 --> 00:19:36.308
"Latte." Lemonade.

00:19:36.308 --> 00:19:37.876
Ugh, I'm losing it. See? I don't,

00:19:37.876 --> 00:19:41.313
I stop drinking caffeine for
a second, and I fall apart.

00:19:41.313 --> 00:19:43.315
Oh, matcha? No!

00:19:43.315 --> 00:19:45.217
No, not matcha!

00:19:45.217 --> 00:19:47.352
Grande matcha lemonade.
All right, lemonade.

00:19:47.352 --> 00:19:50.489
Lemonade is doing all the
heavy lifting on all of these.

00:19:51.423 --> 00:19:52.491
I absolutely hate this.

00:19:52.491 --> 00:19:54.960
Royal English breakfast.

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:56.528
Mm!

00:19:56.528 --> 00:19:57.663
You know what'll help?

00:19:57.663 --> 00:19:58.997
A little caffeine.

00:19:58.997 --> 00:20:00.432
Mm!

00:20:00.432 --> 00:20:01.767
Whoo! All right.

00:20:01.767 --> 00:20:03.635
Also at Starbucks, you can get
something called Refreshers.

00:20:03.635 --> 00:20:05.837
From what I can tell,
they are fruit juices

00:20:05.837 --> 00:20:07.739
with fruit in it. Imagine that.

00:20:07.739 --> 00:20:09.441
I would never normally get a Refresher,

00:20:09.441 --> 00:20:11.610
I just wouldn't think to, but
now I get to try all of them!

00:20:11.610 --> 00:20:13.679
Pink drink!

00:20:13.679 --> 00:20:15.314
Ooh, yeah. Fruity.

00:20:15.314 --> 00:20:19.017
Moving on, we have the
strawberry acai lemonade.

00:20:20.085 --> 00:20:20.919
I like this.

00:20:20.919 --> 00:20:22.988
Similar problem to a
lot of the Frappuccinos.

00:20:22.988 --> 00:20:25.090
One taste, and I'm like,
I could get into it.

00:20:25.090 --> 00:20:26.191
But a whole one of these,

00:20:26.191 --> 00:20:28.760
I feel my gut kind of starting to, blech.

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:31.330
Just the mango dragon fruit, right?

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:32.598
Dragon drink.

00:20:32.598 --> 00:20:36.401
Mango dragon fruit lemonade.

00:20:36.401 --> 00:20:37.970
I think this is the best one so far.

00:20:37.970 --> 00:20:38.804
[beep]

00:20:38.804 --> 00:20:40.939
One second. All right. Don't put that in.

00:20:40.939 --> 00:20:41.773
[beep]

00:20:41.773 --> 00:20:44.643
Moving on, we have the green drink zone.

00:20:44.643 --> 00:20:46.778
Star drink. Assuming star fruit.

00:20:46.778 --> 00:20:47.779
Kiwi star fruit.

00:20:47.779 --> 00:20:50.482
Does lemonade kick it
up even another notch?

00:20:50.482 --> 00:20:52.351
Hm, this one, I like the flavor the best,

00:20:52.351 --> 00:20:53.452
but it's a little strong.

00:20:53.452 --> 00:20:54.486
Yeah, all these are pretty good.

00:20:54.486 --> 00:20:57.589
The last Refresher is the

00:20:57.589 --> 00:20:59.758
strawberry acai.

00:20:59.758 --> 00:21:01.193
They have a regular lemonade

00:21:01.193 --> 00:21:02.661
and a blended strawberry lemonade.

00:21:02.661 --> 00:21:03.962
I mean, come on. Lemonade?

00:21:03.962 --> 00:21:05.964
Everything else that's had
lemonade in it, I've enjoyed.

00:21:05.964 --> 00:21:08.734
So let's just go straight to the source.

00:21:08.734 --> 00:21:09.568
Whoa, dude.

00:21:09.568 --> 00:21:11.570
Starbucks lemonade is, like, really good.

00:21:11.570 --> 00:21:13.105
Is this even in the top
10 things you would get

00:21:13.105 --> 00:21:14.840
at Starbucks, a lemonade? What?

00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:18.443
Now, if you like your lemonade,
a little bit of strawberry.

00:21:19.444 --> 00:21:20.646
This is fantastic.

00:21:20.646 --> 00:21:21.480
Wow.

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:23.849
Even after all these, this is a standout.

00:21:23.849 --> 00:21:25.050
This is really good.

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:26.418
Why is this so good?

00:21:28.854 --> 00:21:29.921
Fantastic.

00:21:29.921 --> 00:21:31.189
Food!

00:21:31.189 --> 00:21:33.191
We have a lot of Indian exclusives.

00:21:33.191 --> 00:21:35.527
I'm going to start with the salads.

00:21:35.527 --> 00:21:37.562
This is a vegetarian grain salad.

00:21:37.562 --> 00:21:40.165
It's got quinoa, it's
got some paneer in it,

00:21:40.165 --> 00:21:44.469
it's got corn kernels that look unborn.

00:21:45.771 --> 00:21:49.074
I'm sure this is super healthy,
but it's also very dry.

00:21:49.074 --> 00:21:51.910
Now the meat version of
it. It's got chicken.

00:21:52.944 --> 00:21:54.946
I'm not really a fan of cold salads.

00:21:54.946 --> 00:21:57.449
If you are a health freak,
you might enjoy this.

00:21:57.449 --> 00:22:01.219
But if you're a fan of
food, you probably won't.

00:22:01.219 --> 00:22:03.388
OK, next up, I'm going to
try all of their rolls.

00:22:03.388 --> 00:22:05.490
Rolls are a huge staple here in India.

00:22:05.490 --> 00:22:07.659
They're one of the most
famous street foods,

00:22:07.659 --> 00:22:10.462
and it's great for the
working-class citizen.

00:22:10.462 --> 00:22:12.898
This is the murgh kathi roll.

00:22:12.898 --> 00:22:15.667
Murgh means chicken in Hindi.

00:22:17.269 --> 00:22:18.970
Oh, that's pretty good.

00:22:18.970 --> 00:22:21.340
Finally! Some spice!

00:22:21.340 --> 00:22:23.842
Oh, my God. This is a life-saver.

00:22:23.842 --> 00:22:25.977
I feel like I'm being brought back to life

00:22:25.977 --> 00:22:28.347
after all those drinks.
This is really good.

00:22:28.347 --> 00:22:30.615
You'll find this only in
India, but honestly, Starbucks,

00:22:30.615 --> 00:22:32.317
you should consider selling this all over,

00:22:32.317 --> 00:22:34.753
because it is tasty.

00:22:34.753 --> 00:22:36.588
Next up is a kakori kebab roll.

00:22:36.588 --> 00:22:40.692
Kakori kebab is basically
minced meat, typically lamb,

00:22:40.692 --> 00:22:44.129
and it's served with a paratha or a roti.

00:22:44.129 --> 00:22:45.297
I've never seen it in a roll,

00:22:45.297 --> 00:22:47.699
and I've never seen it in a pink roll.

00:22:50.035 --> 00:22:51.603
Mm, you can see.

00:22:51.603 --> 00:22:53.205
The main thing about a kakori kebab is

00:22:53.205 --> 00:22:55.140
it should melt in your mouth.

00:22:55.140 --> 00:22:57.042
This has too much of a bite to it.

00:22:57.042 --> 00:22:58.009
Not a fan.

00:22:58.009 --> 00:23:00.379
Next up, chatpata paneer roll.

00:23:00.379 --> 00:23:04.249
Chatpata means full of masala
and flavor, and it's zingy.

00:23:04.249 --> 00:23:06.251
And paneer is cottage cheese.

00:23:06.251 --> 00:23:08.487
We love our cottage cheese here in India,

00:23:08.487 --> 00:23:11.189
and we call it paneer. And you should too.

00:23:11.189 --> 00:23:13.325
Next up, cheese chili toast.

00:23:13.325 --> 00:23:15.260
So, obviously, if you
order this at Starbucks,

00:23:15.260 --> 00:23:17.763
I assume they actually toast
this and the cheese melts

00:23:17.763 --> 00:23:19.030
and it's super delicious.

00:23:20.465 --> 00:23:21.400
I can tell you right now,

00:23:21.400 --> 00:23:23.969
this flavor profile will go
really well with Indians.

00:23:23.969 --> 00:23:25.670
We love our cheese chili toast.

00:23:25.670 --> 00:23:28.707
Monsoon season, mum goes to the kitchen,

00:23:28.707 --> 00:23:32.144
toasts the bread, lot of
butter, some cheese, some chili.

00:23:32.144 --> 00:23:33.945
Bite into it, your mouth's on fire,

00:23:33.945 --> 00:23:36.214
but it's rainy and cold, so you're all OK.

00:23:36.214 --> 00:23:38.850
This is not quite there,
but I feel like it could be.

00:23:38.850 --> 00:23:41.219
Next up, tandoori paneer sandwich.

00:23:41.219 --> 00:23:45.791
I'm gonna have to say that
this bread is a little hard,

00:23:45.791 --> 00:23:47.359
to say the least.

00:23:47.359 --> 00:23:49.327
Might be a bit of an old sandwich.

00:23:50.962 --> 00:23:52.297
Flavor is good, though.

00:23:52.297 --> 00:23:55.300
If I had any of this food
fresh at a Starbucks,

00:23:55.300 --> 00:23:57.269
I might have a very different opinion.

00:23:57.269 --> 00:24:00.305
So far, the paneer items
have been way better

00:24:00.305 --> 00:24:01.807
than the meat items.

00:24:01.807 --> 00:24:02.874
I'm starting to guess there's somebody

00:24:02.874 --> 00:24:05.911
in the Starbucks R&amp;D team
who really likes paneer.

00:24:05.911 --> 00:24:08.180
Sandwiches and protein boxes, here we go.

00:24:08.180 --> 00:24:10.582
You can get a bunch of
exclusive sandwiches,

00:24:10.582 --> 00:24:12.651
US Starbucks, starting right here,

00:24:12.651 --> 00:24:16.922
with the crispy grilled
cheese on sourdough, again.

00:24:16.922 --> 00:24:19.024
Ham and cheese on a baguette.

00:24:19.024 --> 00:24:23.528
Then we get the turkey pesto
with provolone on ciabatta.

00:24:23.528 --> 00:24:25.597
Chicken and bacon on brioche.

00:24:25.597 --> 00:24:26.665
Why is it -- could we get that chicken

00:24:26.665 --> 00:24:27.933
on the whole thing here, guys?

00:24:27.933 --> 00:24:30.569
A focaccia tomato mozzarella.

00:24:30.569 --> 00:24:31.436
At a Starbucks, you can get

00:24:31.436 --> 00:24:34.439
a chicken caprese on ciabatta sandwich.

00:24:34.439 --> 00:24:37.776
On to the protein boxes.

00:24:37.776 --> 00:24:39.678
The chickpea bites and avocado.

00:24:39.678 --> 00:24:41.213
You can tell what's in there.

00:24:41.213 --> 00:24:44.015
Obviously avocado, chickpea bites.

00:24:44.015 --> 00:24:46.384
Egg and cheddar.

00:24:46.384 --> 00:24:47.719
Cheese and fruit.

00:24:47.719 --> 00:24:49.688
Peanut butter and jam.

00:24:49.688 --> 00:24:52.591
Grilled chicken and hummus.
There's your hummus,

00:24:52.591 --> 00:24:54.259
there's your pita, there's
your grilled chicken.

00:24:54.259 --> 00:24:55.293
You can also get,

00:24:55.293 --> 00:24:57.496
which was not available
at the store today,

00:24:57.496 --> 00:24:59.464
egg and Gouda protein box,

00:24:59.464 --> 00:25:01.199
a cheese trio protein box,

00:25:01.199 --> 00:25:03.668
and a cheddar and salami protein box.

00:25:03.668 --> 00:25:08.273
Next up, egg white and
chicken multigrain croissant.

00:25:08.273 --> 00:25:11.676
Should I just call it a
croy-sant to upset people,

00:25:11.676 --> 00:25:13.144
the denizens of the internet?

00:25:14.479 --> 00:25:16.581
If you are somebody trying
to be protein-conscious,

00:25:16.581 --> 00:25:19.150
put on the pounds, this
might be good for you.

00:25:19.150 --> 00:25:22.454
Next up, a masala chicken croissant.

00:25:23.655 --> 00:25:26.825
I guess you can't go
wrong with masala chicken.

00:25:26.825 --> 00:25:28.994
You can go wrong with a croissant.

00:25:28.994 --> 00:25:30.128
This tastes really good.

00:25:30.128 --> 00:25:33.999
Next up, a basil, tomato,
mozzarella sandwich.

00:25:35.433 --> 00:25:38.036
I can imagine just eating
this on a summer day.

00:25:38.036 --> 00:25:38.870
Really yum.

00:25:38.870 --> 00:25:42.607
Next up, creamy spinach and corn pocket.

00:25:42.607 --> 00:25:44.409
Pocket! That's pretty cute.

00:25:44.409 --> 00:25:46.945
As a kid, this was the only
way I enjoyed eating spinach,

00:25:46.945 --> 00:25:49.080
unless it was in palak paneer.

00:25:49.080 --> 00:25:50.515
But right now, I appreciate,

00:25:50.515 --> 00:25:53.184
and I really like it in this pocket.

00:25:53.184 --> 00:25:55.854
Next up, chicken seekh pocket.

00:25:55.854 --> 00:25:58.123
Seekh kebab is basically minced meat,

00:25:58.123 --> 00:26:01.493
and it's sort of pressed onto
a skewer and then grilled.

00:26:01.493 --> 00:26:02.861
Over here, they've done
that, and then they've

00:26:02.861 --> 00:26:05.697
chopped them into little sausage pieces.

00:26:07.332 --> 00:26:10.802
Mm. Minty, it has that pudina flavor,

00:26:10.802 --> 00:26:12.737
a lot of onions that have
just been caramelized,

00:26:12.737 --> 00:26:16.174
so it's sweet but also
spicy. I really like this.

00:26:16.174 --> 00:26:19.277
Starting with the breakfast
sandwiches and wraps,

00:26:19.277 --> 00:26:22.080
the bacon, Gouda, egg. There's
Gouda somewhere on here.

00:26:22.080 --> 00:26:24.049
A sausage, egg, and cheddar.

00:26:24.049 --> 00:26:26.685
The double-smoked bacon,
cheddar, and egg. Dude.

00:26:26.685 --> 00:26:27.819
It's good.

00:26:27.819 --> 00:26:29.487
Ham and Swiss croissant.

00:26:29.487 --> 00:26:31.523
A bacon, sausage, and egg wrap.

00:26:31.523 --> 00:26:32.891
What's up?

00:26:32.891 --> 00:26:33.892
I didn't ...

00:26:35.727 --> 00:26:37.429
Other sandwiches you can get are

00:26:37.429 --> 00:26:39.364
spinach, feta, egg wrap,

00:26:39.364 --> 00:26:40.465
the roasted ham,

00:26:40.465 --> 00:26:42.634
the turkey bacon, cheddar,
and egg white sandwich,

00:26:42.634 --> 00:26:44.869
and the Impossible breakfast sandwich.

00:26:44.869 --> 00:26:45.804
But you know what they do have?

00:26:45.804 --> 00:26:47.205
Bacon and Gruyère.

00:26:47.205 --> 00:26:49.107
Egg white and roasted red pepper.

00:26:49.107 --> 00:26:50.375
Kale and mushroom.

00:26:50.375 --> 00:26:53.411
Get yourself an avocado
spread. For dipping.

00:26:53.411 --> 00:26:54.846
Bagels!

00:26:54.846 --> 00:26:55.981
We got 'em.

00:26:55.981 --> 00:26:57.382
Can I assume this is an everything?

00:26:57.382 --> 00:26:58.550
'Cause it's got everything.

00:26:58.550 --> 00:26:59.718
Cinnamon raisin.

00:26:59.718 --> 00:27:01.586
I can tell because of the raisins.

00:27:01.586 --> 00:27:04.556
Hey, plain. For the New Yorker, right?

00:27:04.556 --> 00:27:06.691
Oatmeal! Oatmeal.

00:27:06.691 --> 00:27:10.061
We got regular, and they
come with a nut medley,

00:27:10.061 --> 00:27:12.063
brown sugar, dried fruit.

00:27:12.063 --> 00:27:15.166
I bet it's like a puck now.
It's been sitting for a while.

00:27:15.166 --> 00:27:16.901
All right. [crew laughing]

00:27:16.901 --> 00:27:18.203
You can also get a blueberry one.

00:27:18.203 --> 00:27:20.405
It's obviously just same
stuff with blueberries.

00:27:20.405 --> 00:27:23.274
Strawberry and overnight grains.

00:27:23.274 --> 00:27:26.578
Next up, a double chocolate chip cookie.

00:27:28.013 --> 00:27:30.715
I think if I put this in a
